./md-review-records/2026-08-09-ghi-info-agent-design-2/dispositions.md:12:   *processed 2026-08-09 → REVISED to the user's drift-notice design, superseding both the remove-and-note and tag-only proposals: a stale pointer in an answer triggers a drift notice back to ghi-info — "you recommended #31, it closed on <date>; double-check and answer again" — one recheck per ask, then the answer is delivered with truthful tags on any closed pointer remaining; nothing is silently removed, so a recheck can surface a successor issue no script could know. Single drift instances never force a reset (that would demand perfection from an LLM); instances count toward the accumulated-drift recycle triggers, which stay as ruled. `--include-closed` remains the deliberate closed-history mode with the same tagging; note lines are written as plain sentences for a zero-context reader. Effectiveness bet (user): tight coupling of notice and recheck ≈ 99.9%, testable at build with probe questions.*
